    <briefdescription>
<para>Challenge-response based liveness detection. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Prevents replay and playback attacks by requiring clients to:<orderedlist>
<listitem><para>Receive a random challenge phrase</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Capture live audio containing that phrase</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Return the audio within a time window</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Prove the response matches the challenge (via speech-to-text)</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
<para>Thread-safe: all methods acquire internal mutex.</para>
<para>The implementation is intentionally fail-closed: opaque or malformed binary payloads are rejected unless they contain a locally verifiable transcript representation. This avoids granting access when upstream capture or speech extraction data is incomplete. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
